  "finding": "The secret-dependent division in the Kyber reference code is emitted as a hardware division instruction in some (vendor, optimisation) cells and replaced by a constant-time reciprocal multiply in others. The two compilers disagree on which cells are safe, so no single build choice is universally safe, which is why a corpus item's label must be bound to a pinned toolchain.",
